## How to Use This Workspace

This project uses a folder-based context system to help AI agents navigate efficiently.

### Key Principle
**Read `CONTEXT.md` before touching any code.** Each task folder contains a `CONTEXT.md` that scopes exactly which files are relevant. Do NOT load the full codebase.

### Folder Guide

| Folder | Purpose | When to Read |
|:---|:---|:---|
| `context/` | Architecture, data models, API specs, decisions | When you need project-level understanding |
| `tasks/current/` | Active task definition + scoped context | When starting work |
| `tasks/backlog/` | Queued tasks | When picking next work |
| `tasks/completed/` | Done tasks (reference) | When checking past decisions |
| `references/` | Deep domain knowledge per module | **JIT only** — when touching that module |
| `scripts/` | Deterministic automation | When running builds, tests, linting |
| `.ai/` | AI-specific rules, prompts, personas | Loaded automatically |

### Workflow
1. Read this file (you're here)
2. Read `PICKUP.md` if resuming a session
3. Read `tasks/current/TASK.md` for what to do
4. Read `tasks/current/CONTEXT.md` for which files to touch
5. Do the work — only touch files listed in CONTEXT.md
6. Update `tasks/current/PROGRESS.md` with decisions and status
7. Update `PICKUP.md` before ending session
